<title>USA: Consumers 67 MW Mich. nuke seen up Thurs.</title>
<headline>Consumers 67 MW Mich. nuke seen up Thurs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Power Co's 67 megawatt Big Rock Point nuclear power plant was expected to resume production Thursday after being shut for repairs, a company spokesman said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;That's what we are shooting for,&quot; spokesman Tim Petrosky said of the planned Oct 31 restart.</p>
<p>The Charlevoix, Mich. plant was shut Oct 23 to correct a problem with a computer program.</p>
<p>Consumers Power is a subsidiary of CMS Energy Corp.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
